  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "In the function $y=1/\\sqrt{x-3}$, the allowable values of the independent variable $x$ are:",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "$x\\ge3$",
    "B": "$x>3$",
    "C": "$x\\ne3$",
    "D": "$x\\le3$"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The expression inside the square root must satisfy $x-3\\ge0$, and the radical expression in the denominator cannot be 0. Therefore, $x-3>0$, that is, $x>3$.",
